NAME
       comm - compare two sorted files line by line

SYNOPSIS
       comm [-123] [--output-delimiter=STR] [--total] [-z]
          file1 file2

DESCRIPTION
       Lines only in file1, only in file2, and in both. The
       files must be sorted (byte order); as in GNU comm, an
       unsorted input is reported and makes the exit status 1.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

